                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 9 at 9:04PM MST until September 9 at 9:45PM MST by NWS Tucson AZ",
                "description": "At 904 PM MST, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nthunderstorms producing heavy rain across the warned area. Between 1\nand 2 inches of rain have fallen. Flash flooding is already occurring\nwith the Babocomari River near Tombstone exceeding bankfull.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and automated gauges.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nWhetstone, Huachuca City, Fairbank and Charleston.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nRoute 90 between mile markers 300 and 313. Route 80 between mile\nmarkers 306 and 313. Route 82 between mile markers 49 and 67.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nSlaughter House Wash, Middle Canyon Wash, Babocomari River,\nEscalante Wash, San Pedro River, Walnut Gulch, Willow Wash and\nClifford Wash.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
